WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.402
-President Trump
did an interview today

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:05.171
where he desperately tried
to rebut allegations

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:07.073
that he broke
campaign finance laws.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.375
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:14.279
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.279 --> 00:00:16.015
It's easy to grow numb

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:18.117
to all the chaos
surrounding President Trump.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:19.619
He has a way
of wearing you down,

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.453
like the guy
in a romantic comedy

00:00:21.453 --> 00:00:23.322
who keeps pushing and pushing
until, finally,

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:24.824
he's standing
outside your house,

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:27.793
trenchcoated with a boom box,
and you think,

00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:30.630
"Yeah, I mean,
I guess this is normal."

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.798
But yesterday was a truly
remarkable day in politics.

00:00:32.798 --> 00:00:35.001
The President's ex-fixer
Michael Cohen

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:36.335
was sentenced
to three years in prison

00:00:36.335 --> 00:00:37.504
for committing crimes

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:39.372
he says the President
told him to commit.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.540
And Cohen was clear
that he now considers himself

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.544
free to tell the full story
of what Trump did.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:47.313
-Michael Cohen said today,
"I take full responsibility

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:49.715
for each act
that I pled guilty to.

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:51.718
The personal ones to me
and those involving

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.686
the President of
the United States of America."

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:56.922
-He said exactly that, today,
no matter what sentence he got,

00:00:56.922 --> 00:00:58.358
would be a day of freedom,

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:02.195
because he was no longer in
the personal and mental prison

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.730
that he was in
working for Donald Trump.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.532
-Wow. You know
you're hard to work for

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:08.268
when going to prison
is a relief.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:09.468
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:11.403
If Andy Dufresne
had worked for Trump,

00:01:11.403 --> 00:01:12.939
he would have pulled
a reverse Shawshank

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.774
and tunneled back into his cell.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.342
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.644
But it really --
[ Applause ]

00:01:18.644 --> 00:01:20.946
It really is
a little bittersweet.

00:01:20.946 --> 00:01:23.216
This is an incredible
fall from grace for these two.

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.384
It was only a few years ago

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:25.885
that Trump
was a reality-TV star,

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.686
a New York City blowhard
who would occasionally

00:01:27.686 --> 00:01:29.755
flirt with running for president
just for the attention.

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:32.525
And Cohen was right by his side,
enjoying the limelight.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.760
He was the Ed McMahon
to Trump's Johnny Carson,

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.562
the Dean Martin
to Trump's Jerry Lewis,

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:38.464
the Salacious Crumb
to Trump's Jabba the Hutt.

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:39.532
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.768
In fact,
here's an interview from 2011

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:44.070
where Cohen clearly enjoys
being Trump's right-hand man

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.672
and bragging about all
the attention Trump was getting.

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:49.642
Although he used an unfortunate
and prescient analogy

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.811
to describe Trump's
political influence.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.213
-We're pleased to be joined
by Michael Cohen,

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:55.715
who's a top lawyer
and right-hand man

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:56.916
for Donald Trump.

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.785
And, Michael, the big question
I got on Twitter,

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:01.054
a lot of people want know,
what is Donald Trump up to?

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.355
Is he running,
is he not running?

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:04.390
Is he gonna play king-maker?
Is he gonna endorse?

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.692
What is the Trump game plan
when it comes to 2012?

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:08.060
-Well, first of all, hi, Rick.
Hi, Amy.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.096
How are you?
Good to see you again.

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:12.531
Donald Trump
is definitely a playmaker.

00:02:12.531 --> 00:02:15.068
I actually
used a statement yesterday --

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:18.103
he is now
the godfather of politics.

00:02:18.103 --> 00:02:19.705
-I'm sorry.
It sounds great,

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:21.708
but Trump is not
the godfather of politics.

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.609
If he were the godfather,
he'd be much better

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:25.745
at getting away
with the stuff he's been doing.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:26.912
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:28.481
He's more like
the naked drunk dude

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:31.283
running down the street on an
episode of "Cops" of politics.

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:33.285
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:33.285 --> 00:02:36.155
Today, Trump did
an interview with Fox News,

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:38.324
where he furiously denied
the allegations.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.159
Now, prosecutors and Cohen
are alleging that Trump

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.094
used "The National Enquirer"
to cover up an affair

00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:44.230
by getting them to pay
for the rights of the story

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.631
and then burying it.

00:02:45.631 --> 00:02:49.068
Late today, NBC News reported
that Trump was in the room

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.570
during the hush-money
discussions

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:51.971
with the tabloid publisher.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:54.707
Trump was asked about that
and claimed it didn't happen,

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:57.710
but he didn't seem
100% sure about it.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:03.316
-"The New York Times" is saying
that a tabloid publisher's deal

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:08.054
to hush money is now
endangering Trump even more.

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:10.022
I'm paraphrasing a little bit.

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:11.090
You know, as you look at this,

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.758
what do you want
the nation to know about

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:14.126
your former attorney being
sentenced yesterday?

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:15.427
-Well, let me just tell you
about the tabloid.

00:03:15.427 --> 00:03:16.796
I don't think --
and I have to go check --

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:19.398
I don't think they even paid
any money to that tabloid.

00:03:19.398 --> 00:03:21.300
-I love how he says
he'd have to check.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.468
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.170
That makes it sound like
he has a ledger somewhere

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:26.072
listing all of his
illegal payments.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:28.607
"Let's see, Mafia, Mafia,
not Putin, Mafia...

00:03:28.607 --> 00:03:30.176
I got nothin'.

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.077
I don't see anything about
a hush payment to a porn star --

00:03:32.077 --> 00:03:33.579
Oh, wait!
Yep, never mind.

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:34.746
It says right here,
'fun stuff.'"

00:03:34.746 --> 00:03:36.682
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:41.687
"It was the fun stuff.
It was fun.

00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:44.123
We had fun."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:46.692
Trump also keeps insisting that
the payments were totally legal

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:48.394
and did not violate
campaign finance law

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:51.063
despite the fact the prosecutors
in his own Justice Department

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:53.132
and independent legal experts
say they did.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:56.736
And to prove it,
he brought along some printouts.

00:03:56.736 --> 00:04:01.373
-And then you have the other
situation, and every lawyer --

00:04:01.373 --> 00:04:06.011
Look -- "Trump didn't violate
campaign finance laws,

00:04:06.011 --> 00:04:07.580
and neither did the President."

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.383
These people writing stories
that Trump did nothing wrong.

00:04:11.383 --> 00:04:14.620
-Oh [bleep] somebody taught
grandpa how to print.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.589
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.023
"Grandpa, what are you doing?"

00:04:18.023 --> 00:04:19.291
"I'm printing!"

00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:22.661
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:25.197
"Printing.

00:04:25.197 --> 00:04:27.433
I like to read my Facebook
in bed."

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:30.702
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.702 --> 00:04:32.137
Fundamentally, for Trump,

00:04:32.137 --> 00:04:34.373
this all comes down
to his relationship with Cohen,

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:36.241
who prosecutors say
was the key figure

00:04:36.241 --> 00:04:38.444
in a criminal scheme to defraud
the American people.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.713
Trump was asked
why he had hired a guy

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:42.581
he now says is a criminal
and a liar,

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:44.316
and he basically shrugged.

00:04:44.316 --> 00:04:47.119
-This was someone who
surreptitiously recorded you.

00:04:47.119 --> 00:04:48.354
-Terrible.

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:50.823
-Is now known
as a criminal liar.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:53.192
Yet this was someone
who was in your inner circle.

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:54.626
-Yeah.
Well, it happens.

00:04:54.626 --> 00:04:55.728
I mean, look, it happens.

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:59.031
-No.
It doesn't just happen.

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:01.334
It only happens to you.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:04.504
No one else accidentally
hires a criminal liar

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:06.338
who pays hush money
to cover up an affair.

00:05:06.338 --> 00:05:08.708
Trump's like a guy who
accidentally admits to something

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:10.876
super embarrassing,
thinking it happens to everyone,

00:05:10.876 --> 00:05:12.478
and then tries to cover it up.

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:14.346
"One time, you know,
I did that thing

00:05:14.346 --> 00:05:17.016
where I got drunk at karaoke,
vomited,

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:19.118
slipped on my own vomit,

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.753
and then my pants split open
in front of them all.

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:22.021
We've all done it, right?"

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:23.589
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:26.258
"Who hasn't been there, right?

00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:29.128
Slipped on vomit,
butt open.

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:31.664
Co-workers there.
You've been there.

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:34.833
You're shaking your head no.
Okay."

00:05:34.833 --> 00:05:37.770
So, today, Trump decided to go
on offense with a TV interview,

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.005
but what was he doing yesterday?

00:05:40.005 --> 00:05:41.707
Well, his ex-fixer
and one-time friend

00:05:41.707 --> 00:05:43.442
was in federal court,
saying the president

00:05:43.442 --> 00:05:44.977
directed him to commit a crime.

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:46.879
Trump is doing what you'd expect

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:48.780
the most powerful man
in the world to be doing --

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:50.816
blowing off work
and watching TV.

00:05:50.816 --> 00:05:52.251
-I have to say,
we just checked.

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:54.020
The President
isn't in the West Wing yet.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.454
There's no Marine guard outside.

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:57.389
So, he's had all morning
to watch TV

00:05:57.389 --> 00:06:00.425
and watch these unfolding
developments in the residence.

00:06:00.425 --> 00:06:02.962
-The President has moved from
the residence to the West Wing.

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:04.797
He arrived here at about noon.

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:06.399
-That's right.
Trump was watching TV

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:08.968
all morning and didn't get
into work until noon.

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:11.170
It's like when you know
you're about to get fired,

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:13.172
so you stop caring
if you're bad at your job.

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:14.307
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:16.008
Soon, Mike Pence
is gonna catch Trump

00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:18.110
smoking weed out back
by the dumpster.

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:21.613
"Hey, Donald, buddy,
you're still on the clock."

00:06:21.613 --> 00:06:23.448
"Whatever, man.

00:06:23.448 --> 00:06:26.118
I'm moving to California
and opening a dispensary."

00:06:26.118 --> 00:06:28.287
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:31.190
But you can't blame Trump for
wanting to hide this one out.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:32.959
Every day,
as his legal problems grow,

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:35.094
Trump is freaking out
because Democrats

00:06:35.094 --> 00:06:36.262
are about to take control
of the House.

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:37.496
Trump has enjoyed two years

00:06:37.496 --> 00:06:38.931
of total Republican control
of the government.

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:41.100
So this is the first time
he's seeing

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.735
what real opposition is like.

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:44.837
It's like he's been playing
tee-ball this whole time,

00:06:44.837 --> 00:06:47.973
and now he has
to face Randy Johnson.

00:06:47.973 --> 00:06:49.675
Although, in reality,

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:51.644
Trump isn't
batting against Randy Johnson.

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:57.583
he's just the bird flying by.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:07:00.753
I know, I know, I know
that's from 2001,

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:02.288
but I didn't have a show then.

00:07:02.288 --> 00:07:04.757
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:06.325
And the bird's fine.

00:07:06.325 --> 00:07:08.661
[ Laughter ]

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:10.329
The bird --
They live together now.

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:11.497
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.497 --> 00:07:14.667
Randy just chucks seeds.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:15.901
Oh, he's a lefty.

00:07:15.901 --> 00:07:18.937
In fact, Republicans
are so scared of Democrats

00:07:18.937 --> 00:07:20.139
having power in Congress,

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:21.774
when they met
in the Oval Office on Tuesday,

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:25.410
Vice President Mike Pence
just went totally silent.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:26.512
In fact,
even after that meeting,

00:07:26.512 --> 00:07:28.480
Pence was supposed
to meet with Republicans

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:30.216
but was mostly quiet.

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:31.217
According to
"The Wall Street Journal,"

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:32.751
"Pence, who looked on silently

00:07:32.751 --> 00:07:34.753
during the public portion
of the Oval Office discussion,

00:07:34.753 --> 00:07:36.488
later met
with Senate Republicans

00:07:36.488 --> 00:07:38.391
at their weekly lunch Tuesday
but said little."

00:07:38.391 --> 00:07:39.725
I think I know
what's going on here.

00:07:39.725 --> 00:07:41.193
Pence wants to be President,

00:07:41.193 --> 00:07:43.695
but doesn't want to associate
himself with any of this mess,

00:07:43.695 --> 00:07:46.598
so he's just hunkered down,
waiting for Trump to resign.

00:07:46.598 --> 00:07:49.101
Look at his body language
in that meeting.

00:07:49.101 --> 00:07:50.402
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.402 --> 00:07:53.105
That's what I do when the guy
next to me on the subway

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:55.374
is loudly watching porn
on his phone.

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:58.009
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.009 --> 00:08:01.213
It looks like Pence is trying
to go full chameleon.

00:08:01.213 --> 00:08:03.649
[ Laughter ]

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:05.017
Trump is facing --

00:08:05.017 --> 00:08:06.719
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:10.690
Trump right now is facing
actual opposition from Congress

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:11.890
for the first time
in his presidency,

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:13.025
and he's clearly rattled.

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:14.793
Every day,
his legal problems get worse.

00:08:14.793 --> 00:08:17.262
If the feds ever knock on his
door and ask him, point blank,

00:08:17.262 --> 00:08:19.098
if he committed a crime,
he'd probably say...

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:20.366
-I have to go check.

00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:22.168
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:08:22.168 --> 00:08:25.872
[ Cheers and applause ]

